    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d461">

                <pb facs="0352" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg348"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/13171: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-09T19:00:00-04:00">June 9, 1938—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>170. Your 278, June 8, 3 p.m., and Department’s 22, December 21, 7 p.m., which
                    quotes final paragraph of Department’s 367, December 21, 7 p.m., to
                        Tokyo.<anchor n="50" xml:id="d461-f1"/></p>
                <p>The Department has sent the following telegram to Tokyo: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Department authorizes approach under conditions and along lines of final
                            paragraph Department’s 367, December 21, 7 p.m.”<anchor n="51"
                                xml:id="d461-f2"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d461-f1" n="50" xml:id="d461-f1-content">
                <p>Telegrams Nos. 22 and 367 not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d461-f2" n="51" xml:id="d461-f2-content">
                <p>For note presented to the Japanese Foreign Office, see telegram No. 822, June 11,
                    10 p.m., from the Consul General at Shanghai, <ref
                        target="frus1931-41v01#pg_599"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >i</hi>, p. 599</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
